  "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[2X-3]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=10.$",
  "worked_solution": "For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+b]=a\\text{E}[X]+b.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-3] & =2\\text{E}[X]-3 \\\\  & =2(10)-3 \\\\  & =17.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
